WEBVTT

00:07.632 --> 00:09.175
[opening theme music playing]

00:39.497 --> 00:43.043
Now, the young master is at Songrim,
this room will be vacant for a while.

00:43.126 --> 00:45.920
Put away his books, clothes,
and all his other belongings.

00:46.004 --> 00:46.963
- Yes, ma'am.
- [Mr. Lee] Go ahead.

00:49.799 --> 00:54.012
He's left to train before, 12 times,
and all 12 times he was sent back.

00:54.596 --> 00:57.056
Shouldn't we wait a few days
in case he comes back again?

00:57.891 --> 00:59.142
This time will be different.

00:59.934 --> 01:02.854
Our young master has really changed.

01:04.147 --> 01:06.983
This room may soon
belong to a married couple.

01:07.067 --> 01:08.735
That's why we're cleaning.

01:08.818 --> 01:10.904
[Mr. Lee] Is the young master promised
to another lady?

01:11.529 --> 01:12.363
[inhales]

01:12.447 --> 01:16.284
If he calls it off again,
it will be hard for him to ever marry.

01:16.367 --> 01:17.869
[maid Kim] It's different this time.

01:17.952 --> 01:21.623
There's a young lady
our young master's quite taken with.

01:21.706 --> 01:22.832
He's in love.

01:23.625 --> 01:25.460
- [Mr. Lee] I see.
- Right, Mu-deok?

01:27.212 --> 01:29.756
You know what I mean. His bird's egg.

01:30.757 --> 01:34.803
I've been thinking
and I'm certain it's the lady in Songrim.

01:34.886 --> 01:35.720
[inhales]

01:35.804 --> 01:38.264
Bird's egg at the very top of a tall tree

01:38.348 --> 01:40.892
sounds like she's aloof.

01:41.476 --> 01:43.269
And he feels protective.

01:43.353 --> 01:46.064
The kind of girl
who is like a white heron.

01:46.147 --> 01:47.190
Like me.

01:47.273 --> 01:48.566
I'm not sure.

01:49.317 --> 01:52.570
When that bird's egg of his
actually hatches,

01:52.654 --> 01:55.573
it may turn out to be
a vicious eagle, not a heron.

01:55.657 --> 01:56.783
[eagle screeching]

01:56.866 --> 01:57.700
You think so?

01:57.784 --> 01:58.618
[gasps]

01:58.701 --> 02:00.245
An eagle would be frightening.

02:01.079 --> 02:03.456
Even a woodpecker or cuckoo would be bad.

02:03.540 --> 02:05.125
There's no use in worrying.

02:05.708 --> 02:08.711
I'm sure when the egg hatches,
it will just fly away.

02:08.795 --> 02:09.629
[bird wings flapping]

02:10.296 --> 02:13.383
How could she do that when she loves him?

02:14.676 --> 02:19.347
If they're so close to each other,
he won't be the only one in love.

02:20.265 --> 02:22.392
The bird's egg would have felt the same.

02:23.726 --> 02:24.769
[maid Kim] Ah!

02:25.270 --> 02:27.397
I really do hope it's Young Lady Heo.

02:28.273 --> 02:29.816
She does look like his mother.

02:31.067 --> 02:31.901
[chuckles]

02:32.443 --> 02:33.278
Oh, Mr. Lee.

02:33.987 --> 02:36.781
Do not touch those.
They belong to Master Jang Gang.

02:37.699 --> 02:38.867
All right. Hurry up.

02:43.163 --> 02:45.290
[Mu-deok] The things Jang Uk and I shared

02:46.416 --> 02:48.543
were a desperation to survive…

02:51.921 --> 02:54.424
and earnest desire to find ourselves…

03:04.142 --> 03:05.643
and a firm promise

03:07.353 --> 03:10.607
that we would part ways
as soon as we got what we wanted.

03:12.609 --> 03:15.278
Even if the affection
Maidservant Kim speaks of…

03:15.361 --> 03:17.238
[reading book]

03:17.322 --> 03:19.532
…is lingering somewhere between us,

03:20.825 --> 03:25.914
it is nothing but a shell
to be discarded once the egg hatches.

03:25.997 --> 03:27.999
[somber music playing]

03:47.644 --> 03:50.939
Did you really memorize all this already?

03:51.022 --> 03:52.982
Yes, and you can check
each and every word.

03:53.650 --> 03:54.817
I didn't miss a single letter.

03:57.862 --> 03:58.905
[Sang-ho] But still,

03:58.988 --> 04:01.241
even if you're quick,
this should at least take a month.

04:01.324 --> 04:02.992
I've had 12 masters in the past

04:03.076 --> 04:05.745
which means I've read
the same books 12 times already.

04:05.828 --> 04:09.290
This is like a total piece of cake for me
at least. Something like that, yeah.

04:09.374 --> 04:12.710
I knew it. I knew it. I wondered
why he was following the rules.

04:12.794 --> 04:14.337
He had his reasons.

04:14.420 --> 04:17.840
So now that I'm free to come and go,
I'm going back home now.

04:18.341 --> 04:19.509
[Jin] You may not leave yet.

04:27.475 --> 04:28.559
Why can't I leave yet?

04:29.143 --> 04:31.145
According to the rules,
since I've mastered the basics,

04:31.229 --> 04:32.272
I should be allowed to go.

04:32.355 --> 04:34.524
The reason I told you to read this book

04:34.607 --> 04:36.651
was to have it engraved
deeply in your heart,

04:36.734 --> 04:38.653
not just for you to memorize it.

04:39.404 --> 04:41.781
However, since you are
sly enough to deceive us,

04:41.864 --> 04:45.159
I don't believe that you've truly mastered
this learning at all.

04:46.744 --> 04:48.162
So, it seems to me that

04:48.871 --> 04:51.749
Songrim's leader can change
the regulations whenever he likes.

04:53.209 --> 04:54.043
For you.

04:54.752 --> 04:56.671
It will be another piece of cake.

04:57.255 --> 04:59.465
I'll allow you to come and go as you like

05:01.175 --> 05:04.137
just as soon as you finish
reading this book.

05:04.220 --> 05:06.264
[playful music playing]

05:07.682 --> 05:08.975
[mouthing]

05:11.394 --> 05:12.228
[sighs]

05:16.482 --> 05:18.359
So, I will actually be allowed to leave

05:19.610 --> 05:21.070
if I just read one book?

05:21.154 --> 05:22.113
That's right.

05:22.989 --> 05:25.783
Go read this book. It should be…

05:26.617 --> 05:29.203
just as easy as eating a piece of cake.

05:29.996 --> 05:31.748
[inhales] Oh, dear!

05:32.415 --> 05:34.250
Mu-deok won't be seeing Uk for a while.

05:38.463 --> 05:39.297
[Jang Uk sighs]

05:48.473 --> 05:50.058
Wait. This book is blank?

05:52.477 --> 05:56.522
It's not blank. There are… words there.

05:57.774 --> 05:58.775
[Jang Uk] Come on, there's nothing.

05:58.858 --> 06:01.069
- You're saying you can read this?
- [chuckles softly]

06:01.736 --> 06:03.196
It's just that you can't see it.

06:04.113 --> 06:06.657
It's Words of the Heart,
by Master Seo Gyeong.

06:06.741 --> 06:09.243
It can only be read
if you focus all your energy.

06:12.955 --> 06:13.790
Hmm.

06:14.874 --> 06:17.376
So you're supposed to see something here?

06:18.002 --> 06:20.505
And I apparently
just can't see it, I guess.

06:25.968 --> 06:27.595
[Beom] Hey, Dang-gu, I heard your friend

06:27.678 --> 06:29.430
didn't even know Words of the Heart.

06:29.514 --> 06:33.059
He's never even had proper training.
Of course, he wouldn't know.

06:33.142 --> 06:37.188
He can't leave the Training Center
until he finishes reading that book.

06:37.271 --> 06:38.356
[Hyo] What will he do?

06:38.439 --> 06:40.399
He will be in there
for at least six months then?

06:41.442 --> 06:43.861
With his skills,
how could he do it in six months?

06:43.945 --> 06:45.947
He might have mastered Ryusu
through pure luck,

06:46.030 --> 06:47.406
but he hasn't been properly trained.

06:48.574 --> 06:50.409
I bet it'll take him over a year.

06:50.493 --> 06:52.120
[laughter]

06:52.203 --> 06:53.454
[book slams]

06:59.836 --> 07:02.463
How would you know
if you've never even read it yourselves?

07:02.547 --> 07:05.424
At least, I know how much training
you need in order to read it.

07:05.508 --> 07:08.010
Then you should also know
just how far ahead of you he is.

07:08.803 --> 07:10.054
Since you haven't received it…

07:11.264 --> 07:12.640
and yet Uk already has.

07:13.850 --> 07:14.851
[scoffs]

07:16.144 --> 07:17.019
[Dang-gu laughs awkwardly]

07:17.770 --> 07:20.523
He's right, guys. You guys shouldn't talk
about things you don't understand.

07:20.606 --> 07:21.441
See ya.

07:23.484 --> 07:24.527
[Beom] Damn it.

07:25.987 --> 07:26.821
[exhales]

07:29.574 --> 07:31.951
Why do you think Uncle
already gave Uk Words of the Heart?

07:32.785 --> 07:34.454
[sighs] I don't know.

07:35.037 --> 07:37.206
As long as he's busy with that,
he can't do anything.

07:37.748 --> 07:38.791
And he's stuck here.

07:38.875 --> 07:41.669
[clicks tongue, breathes deeply]

07:45.631 --> 07:46.466
Well…

07:47.633 --> 07:49.677
I have no intentions of training Jang Uk.

07:50.303 --> 07:54.390
He'll be under my watch, so at least
he won't be able to wander around

07:55.266 --> 07:56.559
causing trouble.

07:56.642 --> 07:59.604
So you didn't accept him into Songrim,

07:59.687 --> 08:01.564
you merely trapped him inside it.

08:03.191 --> 08:05.610
Since we've made
such a show of accepting Uk,

08:06.319 --> 08:07.862
I'm sure his father will come.

08:07.945 --> 08:10.031
By "his father", you mean Jang Gang?

08:10.114 --> 08:12.575
The opening of his son's gate of energy…

08:14.702 --> 08:17.330
was the one thing
Jang Gang feared the most.

08:17.914 --> 08:19.165
If he catches wind of this,

08:20.208 --> 08:22.084
he is certain to come back.

08:22.168 --> 08:23.669
If we're gonna get rid of Jin Mu,

08:24.170 --> 08:26.672
then we will definitely need
the Gwanju to return.

08:26.756 --> 08:27.757
[laughs]

08:27.840 --> 08:29.300
Jang Gang must return…

08:31.135 --> 08:33.179
for all of our problems to be solved.

08:34.931 --> 08:37.058
Anyway, I do take pity on our Uk.

08:37.850 --> 08:39.769
He's already come this far without

08:39.852 --> 08:42.104
any proper training.

08:42.188 --> 08:43.564
But reading that book?

08:43.648 --> 08:45.483
Impossible.
[laughs]

08:53.407 --> 08:55.701
[Sun-i] Why have you prepared
these snacks for him?

08:56.786 --> 08:58.746
I've heard some things
about that Young Master Jang.

08:58.829 --> 09:01.123
He has a complicated family history,

09:01.207 --> 09:03.501
- and he's weak and hot-tempered.
- He's not.

09:05.836 --> 09:06.879
He's a good man.

09:06.963 --> 09:08.631
[laughs]
Okay. How do you know?

09:09.131 --> 09:10.675
I heard he's so difficult

09:10.758 --> 09:13.970
that his servant, Mu-deok, is the only one
who can possibly put up with him.

09:16.222 --> 09:17.765
- Mu-deok?
- Yes.

09:17.848 --> 09:20.810
The girl servant that
Young Master Jang keeps by his side.

09:20.893 --> 09:21.727
That Mu-deok.

09:21.811 --> 09:23.229
[soft music playing]

09:25.982 --> 09:26.941
Hey, Mu-deok.

09:27.817 --> 09:30.486
[Jang Uk] I heard that you stayed
right by my side the whole night.

09:30.570 --> 09:33.698
I thought you were my servant, Mu-deok.
I apologize for my rudeness.

09:35.283 --> 09:37.785
So, that's why he thought
I was Mu-deok that night.

09:39.036 --> 09:39.870
Hmm.

09:44.083 --> 09:44.959
[Sun-i] Good day.

09:45.751 --> 09:47.295
[Sun-i groans]

09:47.378 --> 09:48.796
We are both from Sejukwon.

09:49.672 --> 09:50.631
Let's go, my lady.

10:00.099 --> 10:02.101
[thrilling music playing]

10:14.363 --> 10:16.365
[whimsical music playing]

10:29.128 --> 10:31.380
[stutters]
Uh, but the fire…

10:34.759 --> 10:35.593
[exhales]

10:35.676 --> 10:37.928
[thrilling music playing]

10:50.983 --> 10:53.486
[intense stinger playing]

10:57.740 --> 10:58.699
[Jin] For you.

10:58.783 --> 11:00.409
It will be another piece of cake.

11:00.493 --> 11:01.661
[exhales]

11:02.620 --> 11:03.621
[grunts]

11:05.873 --> 11:07.083
I've been fooled.

11:07.166 --> 11:09.085
Ugh, I can't believe
he tricked me like that.

11:25.351 --> 11:26.185
[gasps]

11:26.268 --> 11:28.104
Uh, we meet again.

11:28.187 --> 11:31.941
Uh, yeah. Are you going somewhere?

11:32.024 --> 11:34.402
Ugh, yeah. There's someone I need to meet.

11:35.820 --> 11:38.447
But why are you going this way?

11:38.531 --> 11:39.365
Uh…

11:40.116 --> 11:41.200
because I am running away.

11:41.784 --> 11:43.160
Ah. [laughs softly]

11:43.244 --> 11:45.996
So… pretend you didn't see this, either.

11:47.039 --> 11:48.290
- [grunts]
- Oh!

11:49.667 --> 11:51.710
[Sun-i] My gosh.
Young Lady Heo is so impatient.

11:51.794 --> 11:53.796
- Honestly. Why did she not wait for me?
- [gasps]

11:53.879 --> 11:55.881
I can't believe she left me behind.

11:55.965 --> 11:57.007
[Yun-ok breathes heavily]

12:00.928 --> 12:01.804
What's the matter?

12:02.304 --> 12:03.139
Huh!

12:03.848 --> 12:05.391
Is Uk not in his room right now?

12:05.975 --> 12:07.560
Oh, no. He's in there.

12:08.269 --> 12:09.520
Then, let's go.

12:09.603 --> 12:13.315
But I… have something to discuss
with Young Master Jang.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.109
I'd like to be alone with him now.

12:17.611 --> 12:20.781
And I think it'll take quite a while,
so wait for me outside.

12:30.875 --> 12:32.877
[soft music playing]

12:37.339 --> 12:38.424
[sighs]

12:40.676 --> 12:43.596
[male servant] Hey, Mu-deok,
a young man has come from Songrim.

12:43.679 --> 12:45.055
He's looking for you.

12:52.354 --> 12:53.689
[pants]

13:02.865 --> 13:04.533
Hello, Young Master Seo.

13:07.203 --> 13:08.829
I guess you must have thought I was Uk.

13:10.789 --> 13:12.625
You probably won't see him for a while.

13:13.709 --> 13:15.544
He has a rather
difficult task to complete.

13:16.295 --> 13:17.755
I'm sure he'll do well.

13:18.672 --> 13:20.758
For now, what's most important for him

13:21.342 --> 13:23.844
is just to stay there and get stronger.

13:24.595 --> 13:27.598
I was worried after you left,
but you seem to be all right.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.518
So, what are you doing
these days without Uk?

13:31.310 --> 13:34.980
I'm a servant,
so my job is to do chores all day.

13:35.856 --> 13:39.568
Maidservant Kim isn't here right now.
So will you wait for her in the study?

13:40.152 --> 13:41.904
I'm not here to see her. I'm here for you.

13:44.031 --> 13:44.949
To see me?

13:46.075 --> 13:48.327
But what business could you
possibly have with me?

13:49.161 --> 13:49.995
Uh…

13:50.829 --> 13:52.039
you have…

13:52.957 --> 13:56.710
my umbrella that I lent you.

13:56.794 --> 13:57.628
[inhales]

13:58.128 --> 13:59.463
Oh, that.

13:59.547 --> 14:02.341
I threw it out
because it ripped on my way back here.

14:03.759 --> 14:04.635
Really?

14:07.054 --> 14:08.013
Then let's go out.

14:08.722 --> 14:09.557
What?

14:09.640 --> 14:10.641
I need a new umbrella.

14:11.308 --> 14:13.936
I want you to buy it.

14:16.564 --> 14:19.358
UMBRELLAS

14:22.611 --> 14:25.447
This one looks exactly like
the umbrella you lent me.

14:25.531 --> 14:26.824
This is made with very…

14:28.868 --> 14:30.536
very low-quality paper.

14:31.203 --> 14:33.372
Mine was made with sheepskin and bamboo.

14:35.040 --> 14:36.375
How nice!

14:37.084 --> 14:39.378
Why did you give
such a nice umbrella to a servant?

14:39.461 --> 14:41.380
I didn't give it. It was a loan.

14:41.463 --> 14:44.216
If you lose someone's belonging,
you should pay for a new one.

14:46.343 --> 14:48.596
And anyway, that was
the only umbrella I had.

14:48.679 --> 14:51.807
Why would the young master
of the Seo family have only one umbrella?

14:51.891 --> 14:53.934
I usually don't go outside when it rains.

14:55.227 --> 14:59.148
My injury from when I was young,
it aches more when it's raining.

15:00.399 --> 15:03.444
The leg you broke,
it still hurts sometimes?

15:07.698 --> 15:10.618
I heard from Young Master Park
that you broke your leg once.

15:12.036 --> 15:13.871
I was injured in Danhyanggok.

15:13.954 --> 15:17.416
How sad that you draw energy
from water but hurt when it rains.

15:18.417 --> 15:20.294
Your leg must not have healed properly.

15:23.213 --> 15:24.173
I had a friend

15:25.466 --> 15:27.259
who had waited for me in Danhyanggok.

15:30.262 --> 15:32.181
She saved me and treated my wound.

15:33.724 --> 15:35.976
It must not have fully healed
because we parted ways…

15:37.519 --> 15:38.854
before I could thank her.

15:46.111 --> 15:47.029
[sighs]

15:49.156 --> 15:49.990
[sighs]

15:52.618 --> 15:54.620
- I like this one.
- What?

15:54.703 --> 15:56.789
I want this one. Go pay for it.

15:58.916 --> 15:59.750
Yes.

16:05.047 --> 16:06.507
- [Mu-deok] This one, please.
- [seller] Of course.

16:06.590 --> 16:09.051
Put it on Master Jang Gang's tab, please.

16:09.635 --> 16:12.513
Why are you putting it on Uk's tab?
You should pay for it.

16:13.138 --> 16:15.557
Gosh, how would a servant like me
have any money?

16:15.641 --> 16:16.809
I know you should have some.

16:17.393 --> 16:19.019
I saw you spending the money you hid

16:19.103 --> 16:21.397
to enjoy yourself and buy nice clothes.

16:21.480 --> 16:22.940
I wasn't that…

16:26.819 --> 16:27.653
[sighs]

16:27.736 --> 16:30.572
- How much?
- [seller] You must have a good eye.

16:30.656 --> 16:33.450
You selected the most
expensive one I have.

16:33.534 --> 16:34.368
[laughs]

16:34.994 --> 16:36.286
[seller clears throat]

16:38.455 --> 16:39.415
[Mu-deok sighs]

16:45.045 --> 16:46.255
[Jang Uk] Mu-deok isn't here?

16:47.423 --> 16:50.300
Where could she have gone
just when I needed her, huh?

16:50.384 --> 16:52.886
Young Master, did you get
kicked out of training again?

16:53.470 --> 16:55.973
I did not! I'm only
just out for a little bit.

16:56.056 --> 16:57.891
And I'm going back soon, okay?

16:57.975 --> 16:58.809
[Mr. Lee] Ah.

16:58.892 --> 17:00.728
Mu-deok will be back soon as well.

17:01.311 --> 17:03.772
Would you like to take
a hot bath while you wait?

17:04.481 --> 17:05.399
Could I?

17:05.482 --> 17:07.901
It's been quite a while
since I last took a bath at my house.

17:07.985 --> 17:09.903
- I'll go get it ready then.
- Hmm.

17:11.822 --> 17:12.656
[exhales]

17:14.450 --> 17:15.284
Hmm?

17:15.951 --> 17:18.203
[playful music playing]

17:26.170 --> 17:27.087
Oh.

17:28.589 --> 17:30.632
Were our honey biscuits always this sweet?

17:32.092 --> 17:32.926
[exclaims]

17:33.010 --> 17:35.387
Why are there no snacks in Songrim?

17:35.971 --> 17:38.098
Even the leader used to have
a sweet tooth.

17:38.766 --> 17:39.600
Hmm.

17:55.282 --> 17:56.533
Are we here today…

17:57.743 --> 17:59.203
so that you can break up with me?

18:00.120 --> 18:01.538
Yes.

18:02.122 --> 18:05.167
In just a bit, the three
gossiping girls will walk by

18:05.250 --> 18:06.460
after floriculture class.

18:06.543 --> 18:09.254
If they see the two of us
fighting when they get here,

18:09.338 --> 18:12.049
they'll spread the rumor of our breakup
everywhere in no time.

18:15.094 --> 18:15.928
[sighs]

18:17.930 --> 18:18.847
As promised,

18:19.598 --> 18:22.017
let's stage it so it looks like my fault.

18:22.643 --> 18:25.020
First, slap me across the face.

18:25.104 --> 18:27.940
Then, when I cling to you, push me away
and storm out through that door.

18:28.023 --> 18:30.567
But that seems a bit extreme.

18:30.651 --> 18:32.361
[Dang-gu] It has to be
to call off a marriage.

18:32.444 --> 18:34.446
We'll need to show
all of them quite a scene.

18:34.530 --> 18:35.447
Make it real.

18:35.531 --> 18:39.034
If we do that, awful rumors
will spread about you, Dang-gu.

18:39.118 --> 18:42.621
If you ruin your reputation,
there'll be no matchmaking for you.

18:45.541 --> 18:46.416
I don't…

18:47.417 --> 18:49.461
want to get married by matchmaking.

18:49.545 --> 18:51.380
[somber music playing]

18:53.090 --> 18:54.675
I want to marry someone…

18:55.968 --> 18:57.094
for love

18:58.762 --> 19:00.764
[soft music playing]

19:04.268 --> 19:05.102
[clears throat]

19:05.853 --> 19:07.187
Slapping is too much, though.

19:08.564 --> 19:11.150
I'll just… throw this at you.

19:11.733 --> 19:14.653
Oh, yeah. Let's do that way, then.

19:17.281 --> 19:18.115
[gasps]

19:18.198 --> 19:19.616
This tea is too hot.

19:20.784 --> 19:22.786
You'll get burnt if I throw it.

19:28.250 --> 19:29.543
Oh! Goodness.

19:30.669 --> 19:31.795
I'll be fine.

19:33.881 --> 19:37.301
I heard people say that
there's a magic show in a few days.

19:39.011 --> 19:40.596
I really want to see it.

19:41.430 --> 19:44.349
But if I break up with you,
I guess I won't be able to.

19:44.975 --> 19:47.227
[stutters] What? Why?

19:47.311 --> 19:51.148
In my experience,
if you ever call off a wedding,

19:52.065 --> 19:54.985
you're expected to
remain at home for a month at least.

19:55.903 --> 19:57.779
Oh, I see.

20:01.992 --> 20:06.163
All right, well, uh, should we delay
breaking up a few days?

20:06.246 --> 20:07.080
Could we?

20:09.208 --> 20:13.295
Uh, but my-my friends will also be there.

20:14.129 --> 20:17.549
So I don't want to go by myself.

20:17.633 --> 20:22.221
Uh, well, since we are still a couple,
then we should go together.

20:23.138 --> 20:23.972
[clears throat]

20:24.473 --> 20:27.226
Well, if you insist.

20:31.813 --> 20:34.566
[Mu-deok] I'll take the pumpkin taffy,

20:34.650 --> 20:36.693
rice taffy, and honey biscuits.

20:36.777 --> 20:37.611
Of course.

20:39.571 --> 20:41.240
The young master is a picky eater,

20:41.740 --> 20:43.867
so he gets cranky if there are no snacks.

20:44.785 --> 20:45.994
Please give these to him.

20:48.997 --> 20:50.832
I like these pine pollen tea snacks.

20:51.375 --> 20:54.002
Of course, you have expensive taste.

20:54.086 --> 20:56.463
- Would you like some of those?
- No.

21:00.717 --> 21:01.760
[clears throat]

21:07.766 --> 21:09.935
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

21:11.937 --> 21:13.355
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

21:13.438 --> 21:16.400
QUALIFICATIONS: HEALTHY, LITERATE,
CAN CALCULATE, NO CRIMINAL RECORD

21:18.860 --> 21:20.737
[seller] I'll put this
on the Jang family's tab.

21:27.411 --> 21:29.079
Please, give this to the young master.

21:29.705 --> 21:33.333
I have some other business
to take care of. Goodbye.

21:50.392 --> 21:51.435
[laughter]

21:52.019 --> 21:53.437
- Yes, ma'am.
- Thank you.

21:54.229 --> 21:55.355
- [buyer] Excuse me.
- [seller] Yes, ma'am?

21:55.439 --> 21:56.565
[So-i] See you later.

22:01.695 --> 22:03.113
[woman 1] It is her, right?

22:03.947 --> 22:05.115
Yes, it is her.

22:05.615 --> 22:06.450
[woman gasps]

22:06.950 --> 22:10.370
- Hey! You stole my purse, didn't you?
- Give me my ring back.

22:11.580 --> 22:12.664
[laughs awkwardly]

22:14.458 --> 22:15.834
[both yell]

22:15.917 --> 22:16.877
[woman 1] Where did she go?

22:16.960 --> 22:19.421
- Hey! Hey! Stop her!
- [woman 2] How dare you!

22:19.504 --> 22:20.672
[woman 2] Stop right there!

22:20.756 --> 22:21.923
[thrilling music playing]

22:22.007 --> 22:23.050
Stop that thief!

22:23.133 --> 22:25.510
- Stop!
- [woman 1] Get back here!

22:25.594 --> 22:28.597
- [grunts]
- Wait until I get my hands on you!

22:28.680 --> 22:30.640
Hey! Hey! Stop! You come back here.

22:31.600 --> 22:33.685
- Hey!
- [man] What's happening here? Hey, hey!

22:33.769 --> 22:35.020
What are you doing?

22:36.730 --> 22:37.814
Catch that thief!

22:37.898 --> 22:40.067
Oh! The path is blocked! What do we do?

22:40.150 --> 22:42.360
- Hey, that's her, right?
- Yeah, yeah.

22:45.739 --> 22:46.948
[So-i pants]

22:49.868 --> 22:50.869
That's Mu-deok.

22:51.411 --> 22:52.245
Mu-deok!

22:56.541 --> 22:57.667
[gasps]

22:57.751 --> 22:59.336
- [woman 1] You!
- [woman 2] There you are, you…

22:59.419 --> 23:01.088
- [woman 2] Hey! Catch that thief!
- [woman 1] Come here!

23:01.171 --> 23:03.632
- Come here.
- [woman 2] Hey, stop right there.

23:04.382 --> 23:06.468
[woman 2] Hey! Come here, come here…

23:10.097 --> 23:11.098
[pants]

23:19.147 --> 23:20.524
It was definitely her.

23:22.400 --> 23:24.236
But how is she able to see, though?

23:34.037 --> 23:36.331
[intense stinger plays]

23:38.041 --> 23:40.335
She used to always wear this
because she couldn't see.

23:42.629 --> 23:43.755
Was it not her?

23:45.215 --> 23:47.175
[ominous music playing]

23:59.646 --> 24:01.690
[suspenseful music playing]

24:02.274 --> 24:03.108
[gasps]

24:03.692 --> 24:05.402
Well, well, I finally found you.

24:06.444 --> 24:07.487
So-i.

24:08.071 --> 24:11.074
I went all the way to Sari Village
because we'd heard you were hiding there.

24:11.158 --> 24:12.784
But you were already gone.

24:13.410 --> 24:15.620
Did you think I wouldn't be able
to find you in the capital?

24:17.414 --> 24:18.331
What's this?

24:19.875 --> 24:23.295
Don't tell me you were pretending
to be blind this time.

24:23.378 --> 24:24.296
[breathes heavily]

24:24.379 --> 24:25.505
[roughneck laughs]

24:25.589 --> 24:28.091
You were always good at
putting up a pitiful front.

24:28.175 --> 24:31.511
But your real specialty is
stabbing people in their back.

24:31.595 --> 24:33.180
[laughs]

24:36.641 --> 24:38.435
How dare you steal money from me?

24:40.520 --> 24:41.980
[softly]
I don't know what you are talking about.

24:42.063 --> 24:42.981
[screams]

24:43.982 --> 24:44.816
[exclaims]

24:46.776 --> 24:48.612
Look at you trying to play me again.

24:48.695 --> 24:49.613
[gasps in pain]

24:50.655 --> 24:51.531
Go.

24:54.075 --> 24:55.493
[screams]

24:56.077 --> 24:57.287
Help me!

24:57.370 --> 24:59.039
Somebody help me!

24:59.122 --> 25:01.291
- [So-i groaning]
- [indistinct chatter]

25:01.374 --> 25:03.627
Somebody help me! I'm blind! I can't see.

25:03.710 --> 25:05.420
- [woman] Oh, dear!
- I don't know any of them,

25:06.171 --> 25:09.299
but these strange men are trying
to kidnap me! Please!

25:09.925 --> 25:12.886
[shouts] Someone, anyone, help me!

25:12.969 --> 25:15.555
Look at you trying real hard.

25:15.639 --> 25:17.307
[screams]

25:17.933 --> 25:18.934
Help me!

25:19.017 --> 25:20.769
[roughneck] What are you all
looking at, huh?

25:21.353 --> 25:23.271
- Come here.
- [So-i screams]

25:24.105 --> 25:25.106
[groans]

25:27.609 --> 25:29.444
[intense music playing]

25:33.949 --> 25:36.493
You cannot drag people off
against their will.

25:37.619 --> 25:39.829
[roughneck] I have a good reason
for doing this,

25:40.372 --> 25:41.831
so just be on your way.

25:42.540 --> 25:44.376
Please, sir! I cannot see anything.

25:44.459 --> 25:46.419
- And I don't even know who they are.
- [roughneck] You little--

25:46.503 --> 25:47.587
[yelps]

25:49.047 --> 25:50.298
- Get him!
- [men shouting]

25:54.761 --> 25:55.595
[grunts]

25:56.846 --> 25:58.014
[yells, grunts]

26:01.476 --> 26:02.310
[roughneck gasps]

26:02.394 --> 26:04.104
He's… he's a mage.

26:04.187 --> 26:05.021
Run!

26:13.613 --> 26:14.990
Are you able to stand?

26:20.245 --> 26:21.788
Thank you very much, sir.

26:21.871 --> 26:23.248
They look like dangerous men.

26:23.748 --> 26:25.959
You should properly go report it
to the authorities and get help.

26:26.835 --> 26:27.711
I'll take you.

26:27.794 --> 26:30.588
I'm all right. I don't need them.

26:32.382 --> 26:33.758
Your cane is broken.

26:40.390 --> 26:41.349
It's an umbrella.

26:42.392 --> 26:43.685
You can take this instead.

26:58.158 --> 26:58.992
[sighs]

27:00.618 --> 27:03.204
Excuse me, sir, best to let her be.

27:03.288 --> 27:05.832
She refused to let you
take her to the authorities.

27:05.915 --> 27:08.209
I don't know her situation, young man,

27:08.293 --> 27:10.045
but I do know those guys were thugs.

27:10.712 --> 27:12.797
No good will come
out of involving yourself

27:12.881 --> 27:14.090
in their affairs.

27:24.601 --> 27:25.643
[Seo Yul] I'll take you.

27:26.519 --> 27:28.938
You should properly go report it
to the authorities and get help.

27:33.234 --> 27:34.986
Maybe I should have said yes then.

27:36.529 --> 27:37.405
[chuckles]

27:45.330 --> 27:47.499
[eerie music playing]

27:56.132 --> 27:59.135
Number 125.

28:00.220 --> 28:02.722
Is this the number of people
who have already applied?

28:02.806 --> 28:04.140
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE

28:05.266 --> 28:07.018
And they're only going to hire five.

28:08.353 --> 28:09.938
Do I have a chance?

28:10.939 --> 28:11.773
[Mr. Lee] Hey, Mu-deok.

28:13.858 --> 28:14.901
Oh, here you are.

28:14.984 --> 28:16.444
The young master's looking for you.

28:16.528 --> 28:18.988
Young Master Seo came by again?

28:19.072 --> 28:21.157
Not him. Young Master Jang Uk.

28:21.908 --> 28:24.828
Young Master Jang snuck
out of Songrim to come back home.

28:24.911 --> 28:26.621
[soft music playing]

28:29.457 --> 28:30.542
[sighs]

28:34.129 --> 28:37.006
Huh, I need to be back before sundown.
Where could she be?

28:41.386 --> 28:43.388
[soft music continues playing]

28:48.309 --> 28:49.144
[exhales]

29:01.823 --> 29:02.657
[sighs]

29:05.535 --> 29:06.369
[clicks tongue]

29:15.670 --> 29:17.130
[panting]

29:20.300 --> 29:21.426
Where is he?

29:21.509 --> 29:23.678
He just left. I didn't see him, either.

29:26.306 --> 29:28.850
He said he'd be obedient, but he ran away.

29:30.143 --> 29:31.936
I hope he got back without getting caught.

29:32.729 --> 29:33.563
[breathes heavily]

29:35.023 --> 29:36.065
He was just here.

29:36.941 --> 29:37.942
Just now.

29:39.944 --> 29:41.654
What is with that girl?

29:41.738 --> 29:43.782
[soft music playing]

30:06.137 --> 30:06.971
Jang Uk.

30:07.889 --> 30:08.807
Look, Young Master!

30:08.890 --> 30:10.892
[romantic music playing]

30:13.561 --> 30:16.314
Where have you been?
I thought I couldn't see you.

30:35.291 --> 30:36.543
[chuckles softly]

30:45.426 --> 30:47.762
But now, I've seen you. I'm very glad.

30:50.348 --> 30:52.809
I have to go back now,
or I'll get in trouble.

30:53.726 --> 30:56.354
Just wait there. I'll be there soon, too.

30:58.022 --> 30:59.065
I found a way.

30:59.148 --> 31:02.235
Could you stay focused
on what you need to do in there?

31:02.318 --> 31:04.028
And I'll do everything I can out here.

31:05.446 --> 31:08.074
All right. But what's the way, though?

31:09.534 --> 31:11.369
I heard Songrim is hiring servants.

31:11.452 --> 31:13.162
[romantic music continues playing]

31:32.056 --> 31:33.266
Be safe. Don't get caught.

31:59.292 --> 32:02.503
[eunuch] Your Highness,
instead of going to Sejukwon yourself,

32:02.587 --> 32:05.173
you should summon
Master Heo to the palace.

32:06.090 --> 32:08.968
That's all right.
It gives me a reason to get out.

32:09.469 --> 32:10.929
[Go Won] It helps my recovery.

32:17.018 --> 32:18.061
Is that Jang Uk?

32:28.363 --> 32:29.864
What are you doing out here?

32:29.948 --> 32:31.824
I heard you weren't allowed
to leave the Training Center

32:31.908 --> 32:33.826
until you're able to read
The Words of the Heart.

32:33.910 --> 32:36.329
Last time, you followed me
to where I was drinking.

32:36.412 --> 32:38.665
And now it looks like
you're keeping tabs on me.

32:38.748 --> 32:40.291
Why do you seem so interested in me?

32:40.375 --> 32:41.960
It makes me uncomfortable.

32:42.043 --> 32:44.045
Master Heo from Sejukwon told me about it.

32:45.004 --> 32:48.633
Right. I heard you fell ill
from drinking the liquor I gave you.

32:48.716 --> 32:51.010
Why did you come all the way
to Sejukwon, Your Highness?

32:51.719 --> 32:54.681
Wait, don't tell me it still hurts.

32:55.181 --> 32:57.392
Are you still in pain
from where I hit you? Oh, my goodness.

32:57.475 --> 33:00.186
No, not at all. I'm completely fine now.

33:00.687 --> 33:02.855
I just go there to get
some supplements. That's all.

33:02.939 --> 33:03.815
[Jang Uk] Hmm.

33:03.898 --> 33:05.692
I hope you take
many good supplements, sire.

33:05.775 --> 33:07.360
You must live a long, healthy life.

33:08.111 --> 33:08.945
[Jang Uk laughs]

33:09.445 --> 33:12.031
Wait! What were you
trying to hide over there?

33:13.282 --> 33:14.200
Let me see it.

33:16.619 --> 33:18.913
[suspenseful music playing]

33:31.843 --> 33:32.885
It's a honey biscuit.

33:33.803 --> 33:36.139
I wanted to eat it myself.
How did you know I had it on me?

33:36.723 --> 33:37.598
You can have it.

33:44.188 --> 33:47.275
Songrim doesn't have
these kinds of snacks.

33:48.860 --> 33:49.861
Did you go home?

33:49.944 --> 33:51.571
[suspenseful music playing]

33:54.699 --> 33:55.533
[chuckles]

33:56.784 --> 33:59.912
You know you'll be in trouble
if anyone finds out you ran back home.

34:00.538 --> 34:03.791
You gave me a drink as congratulations
and even complimented me last time.

34:03.875 --> 34:06.836
Would you r-really tattle on me now
for sneaking out?

34:10.465 --> 34:12.884
I… gave you my honey biscuit.

34:18.222 --> 34:22.602
Well, stay away from that big pine tree.
I saw some mages there.

34:25.563 --> 34:27.690
Thank you very much, Your Highness.
All the best for you.

34:31.986 --> 34:33.738
I don't understand why I'm so nice to him.

34:38.576 --> 34:39.702
This is delicious.

34:40.828 --> 34:41.662
Is it really?

34:46.084 --> 34:47.043
Is it tasty?

34:48.461 --> 34:50.421
[queen] I thought that the Crown Prince

34:51.297 --> 34:53.925
would be more hostile
to Songrim after the match.

34:55.176 --> 34:56.969
Instead, he sheathed his sword

34:57.762 --> 34:59.931
and become even closer to them.

35:00.556 --> 35:03.810
He must have decided to befriend them
so they could be useful

35:03.893 --> 35:05.520
when he becomes the next king.

35:07.230 --> 35:10.608
Are you certain we shouldn't step in?

35:10.691 --> 35:11.943
Do not worry.

35:12.026 --> 35:13.986
We can change his mind quite easily.

35:14.612 --> 35:16.948
After all, we do have
Jang Uk's constellation plate.

35:18.741 --> 35:21.953
The Crown Prince will have no choice
but to kill him eventually.

35:33.172 --> 35:37.760
Is that it? This is what
we'll use to subdue Jin Ho-gyeong?

35:37.844 --> 35:41.180
The power of Jinyowon
will finally be within our grasp.

35:41.264 --> 35:43.266
[suspenseful music playing]

36:01.826 --> 36:04.370
It's been nearly four hours
since Young Lady Heo went inside.

36:05.788 --> 36:07.039
Oh!

36:07.123 --> 36:08.374
Don't bother them.

36:08.457 --> 36:09.792
They have a lot to talk about.

36:12.962 --> 36:16.299
Oh! Hey! Hey! Hey, wait! Stop!

36:17.592 --> 36:19.552
You really shouldn't bother them.

36:19.635 --> 36:20.803
Something's wrong.

36:20.887 --> 36:23.097
I should see whether
Jang Uk's really in there.

36:23.181 --> 36:25.391
Are you seriously doubting
what my lady said?

36:27.310 --> 36:28.311
Oh…

36:29.979 --> 36:30.897
[sighs]

36:30.980 --> 36:32.523
Why isn't he back yet?

36:34.734 --> 36:38.279
If they find out he is gone,
it'll be so embarrassing.

36:41.407 --> 36:42.366
[footsteps approaching]

36:45.912 --> 36:46.746
[gasps]

36:48.289 --> 36:50.166
What are you doing here?
I thought you'd be gone.

36:51.125 --> 36:52.877
I told them we were together in here

36:52.960 --> 36:55.296
so they wouldn't realize
you'd left on your own.

36:56.339 --> 36:58.216
I've been waiting here
for you to get back.

37:01.928 --> 37:02.929
[Sun-i exhales]

37:04.764 --> 37:07.600
Hah, see? They are here
together just like she said.

37:09.810 --> 37:11.145
I'm going to leave now.

37:11.646 --> 37:14.732
I enjoyed our conversation today.

37:16.108 --> 37:17.318
Oh, yes.

37:17.902 --> 37:18.736
[Jang Uk] Mm-hmm.

37:19.779 --> 37:20.613
Oh.

37:29.705 --> 37:31.958
What were you doing
in here for four hours?

37:33.376 --> 37:34.293
Good question.

37:35.378 --> 37:36.212
What were…

37:37.296 --> 37:38.965
we doing here for that long?

37:41.676 --> 37:43.719
[whimsical music playing]

37:54.438 --> 37:55.314
[sighs]

38:01.320 --> 38:02.738
She must have been bored, huh?

38:03.489 --> 38:04.323
[scoffs]

38:07.159 --> 38:09.620
You want to enter
into Songrim's hiring contest?

38:09.704 --> 38:12.248
Yes. Look at what happened today.

38:12.331 --> 38:16.627
Young Master Jang Uk clearly needs me
right by his side at all times.

38:17.503 --> 38:18.421
I have to agree.

38:19.171 --> 38:22.800
How uncomfortable must he have been
to come here to bathe and eat snacks.

38:23.634 --> 38:26.929
Our young master is very sensitive
and was doted on growing up.

38:27.013 --> 38:29.223
So living with others
in Songrim doesn't suit him.

38:29.807 --> 38:31.058
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE

38:31.142 --> 38:32.351
I've already put my name in.

38:33.269 --> 38:34.395
I'll get in no matter what.

38:35.396 --> 38:37.273
Yeah, you don't need that.

38:37.982 --> 38:39.483
This is the Jang family.

38:39.567 --> 38:41.027
We can easily put you in there.

38:41.110 --> 38:42.570
[gasps] Is that true?

38:42.653 --> 38:45.656
So then, does that mean
that I won't have to take the test at all?

38:45.740 --> 38:48.284
Of course not. Just trust me.

38:51.495 --> 38:52.830
That is not possible.

38:53.622 --> 38:57.460
Songrim's servants are only ever chosen
through open recruitments.

38:57.543 --> 38:58.794
There are no exceptions.

38:58.878 --> 39:00.588
Ah, she doesn't need a free post.

39:01.255 --> 39:03.883
Just the entrance plaque.
Just write up her name

39:03.966 --> 39:05.551
so she can have one.

39:05.634 --> 39:07.386
The Jang family will pay her salary.

39:07.970 --> 39:09.138
[exhales]

39:10.931 --> 39:12.016
Also…

39:12.850 --> 39:14.518
here.
[inhales]

39:15.353 --> 39:18.564
I thought it would suit you,
Maidservant Park, so I bought you one.

39:19.148 --> 39:19.982
Huh?

39:20.066 --> 39:22.234
[quirky music playing]

39:23.402 --> 39:24.612
Here.

39:26.238 --> 39:27.281
Hmm.

39:30.951 --> 39:31.869
[exasperated sigh]

39:36.457 --> 39:38.459
[tense music playing]

39:48.427 --> 39:49.887
[comical music playing]

39:50.971 --> 39:54.642
Word has it that you bribed
Maidservant Park of Songrim

39:55.810 --> 39:57.436
with this simple favor.

39:57.520 --> 40:00.981
- It was not a big deal, just a gift.
- I heard that you asked her

40:02.108 --> 40:04.402
to secure a position there for Mu-deok.

40:04.485 --> 40:07.530
Well, since our young master
is so sensitive,

40:07.613 --> 40:09.532
I thought having Mu-deok close by

40:09.615 --> 40:11.200
would help him improve
his training process,

40:11.992 --> 40:13.619
so I asked her for a favor.

40:15.162 --> 40:16.956
So then, this truly was a bribe!

40:17.748 --> 40:21.043
I apologize. I guess
I wasn't thinking clearly.

40:21.127 --> 40:23.170
When Maidservant Park brought this to me,

40:23.254 --> 40:26.090
I defended you by telling her
you would never actually

40:26.882 --> 40:28.008
do such a thing.

40:28.092 --> 40:32.096
How will I ever dare face
Maidservant Park ever again?

40:32.179 --> 40:33.431
I…

40:35.850 --> 40:36.684
Um…

40:37.810 --> 40:39.979
I will go and apologize to her.

40:40.813 --> 40:42.022
What will everyone think?

40:42.857 --> 40:46.318
They'll definitely think that
you abused your relationship with me

40:46.402 --> 40:48.279
to bribe someone to get what you wanted.

40:48.362 --> 40:51.824
It's true I did give her that scarf,
but I never mentioned your name to her.

40:51.907 --> 40:53.075
Even still,

40:53.159 --> 40:55.786
everyone in Songrim knows
that you and I are close.

40:55.870 --> 40:59.540
If you act like this,
then I can no longer afford…

41:03.043 --> 41:06.964
to continue having
such a close relationship any longer.

41:08.799 --> 41:12.511
Sure! In that case,
I'll just stop coming here.

41:13.846 --> 41:15.890
And besides, maybe our relationship

41:15.973 --> 41:18.601
was never really as deep as
you like to say it was, you know.

41:19.226 --> 41:21.020
Because if we were truly that close,

41:21.103 --> 41:24.148
you would never have mentioned
cutting ties with me so easily, right?

41:24.231 --> 41:25.065
Fine.

41:26.275 --> 41:29.612
- Well, I…
- I'll go to Maidservant Park

41:29.695 --> 41:32.114
and tell her that I, who bribed her,

41:32.198 --> 41:33.616
I am not-- not close at all

41:34.158 --> 41:36.827
with the great leader of Songrim.
I never really had been.

41:36.911 --> 41:38.204
- L-Look, Maidservant--
- Yes…

41:38.787 --> 41:40.247
I'm so terribly sorry

41:40.873 --> 41:42.333
that I embarrassed you this way.

41:43.125 --> 41:44.502
Wait, Maidservant Kim.

41:46.378 --> 41:47.755
You can't just leave like that.

41:55.387 --> 41:56.388
You should take this.

41:58.349 --> 42:01.852
If I were to keep it,
I'd be accepting a bribe.

42:06.899 --> 42:08.776
[whimsical music playing]

42:10.361 --> 42:11.529
[maid Kim grunts softly]

42:15.741 --> 42:16.575
[grunts]

42:18.744 --> 42:20.204
Also, that is…

42:21.247 --> 42:23.457
You said you'd stop coming.

42:23.958 --> 42:24.792
Um…

42:25.459 --> 42:28.128
that wasn't what I… meant.

42:28.712 --> 42:29.797
Oh, Maid--

42:29.880 --> 42:31.549
Wait! Where are you…

42:31.632 --> 42:32.841
[grunts]

42:34.218 --> 42:35.094
[sighs]

42:36.887 --> 42:38.097
This is hard.

42:44.186 --> 42:45.062
[sighs]

42:55.990 --> 42:57.283
[Master Lee] You can't do it yet.

43:00.369 --> 43:01.370
Master Lee.

43:02.037 --> 43:04.873
You can't read that book
with the concentration you have right now.

43:05.624 --> 43:08.794
Because you've never trained
as diligently as the others have.

43:08.877 --> 43:11.880
And how long will it take
if I start my training now?

43:12.506 --> 43:14.383
Well, if you're quick, a year.

43:15.426 --> 43:18.637
I-I cannot do that. I can't spend
a whole year just trapped here.

43:18.721 --> 43:21.849
I think that's exactly the reason
why Park Jin gave you that book.

43:24.184 --> 43:25.019
[sighs]

43:26.520 --> 43:27.855
You could shorten it

43:28.606 --> 43:32.359
if you become my pupil
and receive my tutoring.

43:32.443 --> 43:33.277
You…

43:34.987 --> 43:36.697
mean by drinking the chaste herb tea?

43:39.950 --> 43:42.286
Just give me
a little bit of time to think.

43:43.704 --> 43:46.123
This book, The Words of the Heart

43:46.206 --> 43:50.544
contains a poem written
by my master, Seo Gyeong himself.

43:50.628 --> 43:51.795
Poem?

43:51.879 --> 43:53.714
And it's not that long.

43:54.882 --> 43:57.134
Once you're finally able
to read the first word,

43:57.217 --> 43:59.511
you'll find that the rest comes easily.

44:00.971 --> 44:03.724
Ah, but you can't see it.

44:04.767 --> 44:06.143
Are you having fun teasing me now?

44:06.226 --> 44:07.728
It's not like you're going
to tell me about it.

44:07.811 --> 44:09.104
It's amusing to watch.

44:09.188 --> 44:10.356
[Master Lee chuckles softly]

44:11.106 --> 44:13.609
Should I help you another time?

44:15.486 --> 44:16.320
Yes.

44:17.237 --> 44:20.491
Let me tell you one secret
about this book that no one knows.

44:21.909 --> 44:23.702
The poem transcribed here is…

44:24.662 --> 44:25.496
a love letter.

44:27.081 --> 44:28.457
A… love letter?

44:28.540 --> 44:29.583
Correct.

44:29.667 --> 44:31.794
Countless mages have been asked
to read this book,

44:31.877 --> 44:33.587
but no one knows it's a love letter.

44:34.505 --> 44:35.631
Ah.

44:37.508 --> 44:41.553
Master Seo Gyeong originally wrote this
for a lady who could not see

44:41.637 --> 44:44.473
so that she would be able
to read it with her heart instead.

44:49.103 --> 44:52.314
You can read it by training
your concentration skills.

44:52.398 --> 44:57.069
But now that you know what it is,
try to think of another way to read it.

44:57.986 --> 45:01.698
How do you think
a love letter is supposed to begin?

45:08.956 --> 45:10.124
What is this thing?

45:13.127 --> 45:14.378
Was he a pervert?

45:14.461 --> 45:18.048
Why would anybody want to
make others read his own love letter, huh?

45:18.549 --> 45:21.260
Oh, why must I read this?
I can't even see it at all.

45:22.094 --> 45:23.387
Was he really a pervert?

45:23.929 --> 45:24.972
[sighs]

45:26.598 --> 45:31.019
Master Lee, it's getting colder.
Instead of returning to Danhyanggok,

45:31.103 --> 45:34.231
why don't you just stay here?
I'll take good care of you.

45:34.314 --> 45:35.607
- [laughs]
- No.

45:36.108 --> 45:38.986
My training cannot be accomplished
by wearing warm clothes

45:39.069 --> 45:40.821
- and living in comfort.
- Ah.

45:40.904 --> 45:43.282
Master Lee, you know as your pupil,

45:43.365 --> 45:46.577
I just want my master to be warm.
[laughs]

45:48.662 --> 45:51.540
It seems that you've truly matured.

45:52.291 --> 45:53.125
[laughs awkwardly]

45:59.715 --> 46:01.175
[soft music playing]

46:01.258 --> 46:02.759
[heart pounding]

46:08.932 --> 46:12.144
Oh, that's Maidservant Kim
of the Jang family.

46:12.728 --> 46:15.731
Given how unhappy she looks,
she and Jin must have argued.

46:17.316 --> 46:19.109
Oh. Hello.

46:19.193 --> 46:20.110
[laughs]

46:23.697 --> 46:24.907
Master Lee.

46:25.824 --> 46:28.160
Why did you leave so quickly last time?

46:28.243 --> 46:29.953
I didn't even get a chance to thank you.

46:30.037 --> 46:33.248
I take it you two have met before?

46:33.874 --> 46:36.585
That's right. We met
at the celebration at Chwiseonru.

46:36.668 --> 46:37.586
- [laughs]
- [maid Kim] Oh.

46:37.669 --> 46:39.171
I wanted to ask you about your clothes.

46:39.254 --> 46:40.964
Your seam burst because of me.

46:41.048 --> 46:42.090
[Master Lee grunts]

46:42.758 --> 46:43.800
I'm all right.

46:44.468 --> 46:45.719
What seam?

46:45.802 --> 46:47.095
Ah, I see.

46:47.679 --> 46:48.805
It's very cold out.

46:48.889 --> 46:50.766
Are you not too cold
in those thin clothes?

46:51.767 --> 46:53.560
Why don't you wear this, at least?

46:54.144 --> 46:56.522
I wanted to give you something
to say thank you.

46:59.608 --> 47:02.694
Also, know this is
not a bribe, it's a gift.

47:02.778 --> 47:03.654
Here.

47:04.488 --> 47:06.657
[uplifting music playing]

47:22.673 --> 47:23.507
Ah.

47:24.007 --> 47:25.300
It really suits you.

47:34.184 --> 47:35.018
[Heo Yeom] Uh…

47:35.102 --> 47:38.522
are you okay with being warm?

47:47.114 --> 47:51.285
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

47:52.494 --> 47:53.912
[indistinct chatter]

47:54.454 --> 47:58.750
We will begin
the Songrim Servant Hiring Contest

47:58.834 --> 48:02.754
to decide on five applicants who
will have the honor to work in Songrim.

48:03.338 --> 48:05.591
[maidservant Park]
I will read the list of applicants.

48:06.300 --> 48:08.552
Answer me when I call your names.

48:11.430 --> 48:13.515
Number one, Park Jun-hwa.

48:13.599 --> 48:14.433
Here.

48:15.058 --> 48:16.977
And two, An So-jeong.

48:17.060 --> 48:18.145
Here!

48:19.938 --> 48:21.023
An So-jeong.

48:21.106 --> 48:22.357
TWO

48:22.441 --> 48:23.442
An…

48:23.525 --> 48:24.484
[clears throat]

48:25.110 --> 48:27.446
- Three, Lee Yeong-ok.
- [Yeong-ok] Here.

48:27.529 --> 48:29.823
- Four, Park Hyeon-su.
- [Hyeon-su] Here.

48:30.407 --> 48:32.701
- Five, Bae Hui-young.
- [Hui-young] Here.

48:35.203 --> 48:36.038
[Dang-gu clears throat]

48:38.582 --> 48:39.416
Huh?

48:40.083 --> 48:41.168
What is this for?

48:41.251 --> 48:42.753
I'm looking just in case.

48:46.548 --> 48:48.884
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE, MU-DEOK

48:50.135 --> 48:51.470
[chuckles softly] There she is.

48:51.970 --> 48:54.848
Number 125. Is Mu-deok here?

48:56.266 --> 48:57.309
Over here!

49:02.481 --> 49:06.401
Your servant, Mu-deok,
is here in Songrim today.

49:07.736 --> 49:09.363
I'm saying this for your sake.

49:09.446 --> 49:10.947
Don't even think of trying to leave here.

49:11.031 --> 49:12.407
[in loud voice]
Could you please be quiet?

49:15.285 --> 49:16.828
[in normal tone]
Could you be quiet, please?

49:16.912 --> 49:19.373
I need to concentrate
in order to be able to read this.

49:19.456 --> 49:20.874
[whispers] I'll let you be then.

49:23.210 --> 49:24.044
[laughs softly]

49:25.128 --> 49:25.962
[grumbles]

49:34.388 --> 49:38.141
[Heo Yeom] Then, I'll see you
in three days, Your Highness.

49:38.225 --> 49:42.062
By the way, why is Songrim
so busy today? Seems crowded.

49:42.813 --> 49:47.150
A contest. They're going to
pick servants for housekeeping today.

49:47.943 --> 49:50.612
- Songrim makes a contest of that?
- [eunuch] Your Highness.

49:51.196 --> 49:53.490
Being a Songrim's servant
is a coveted position.

49:53.573 --> 49:54.408
When I looked,

49:54.491 --> 49:56.702
I saw the Jang family's servant there,
Your Highness.

49:58.078 --> 50:00.163
- Filthy Mu-deok?
- Yes, sire.

50:01.248 --> 50:03.333
[intense music playing]

50:13.552 --> 50:15.095
The first test you'll face

50:15.679 --> 50:20.225
will test the strength
of your reading and arithmetic skills.

50:21.017 --> 50:22.728
You'll have to get full marks to pass.

50:22.811 --> 50:25.480
Get just one question wrong,
and you're disqualified!

50:25.564 --> 50:26.523
[coughs]

50:29.067 --> 50:30.902
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

50:33.739 --> 50:35.574
Yul! Yul!

50:35.657 --> 50:36.908
[pants]

50:38.076 --> 50:38.952
I found the test.

50:41.329 --> 50:43.832
- So many questions. Even writing.
- [sighs]

50:44.541 --> 50:47.210
Mu-deok is smart,
but can she answer them all?

50:50.756 --> 50:51.715
[Go Won] This is pretty hard.

50:52.215 --> 50:55.010
Eunuch Oh, what do you use
to wash clothes stained with ink?

50:55.093 --> 50:56.136
That's a question.

50:56.219 --> 50:58.680
For ink-stained clothes,
rice paste does the trick.

50:59.306 --> 51:00.557
[Go Won] What do you do with it?

51:00.640 --> 51:03.477
Well, first, you apply it
to the stain, and then you can…

51:08.440 --> 51:09.274
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

51:09.357 --> 51:12.694
[Seo Yul] "You have invited
20 guests each from 3 different families."

51:12.778 --> 51:16.156
"One table seats four people.
How many tables do you need to provide?"

51:16.239 --> 51:17.073
[inhales deeply]

51:18.033 --> 51:21.578
Twenty people from
three families, 60 total.

51:23.663 --> 51:27.083
Each table can fit four people,

51:28.168 --> 51:30.253
- so it's fifteen.
- No, no, no.

51:30.337 --> 51:32.380
They said "three families" on purpose.

51:33.298 --> 51:37.344
Each family must push
their tables together.

51:38.053 --> 51:40.388
We need more tables
if they're pushed together.

51:40.472 --> 51:42.766
Each family needs nine tables.

51:44.059 --> 51:45.101
NINE × THREE = TWENTY-SEVEN

51:45.185 --> 51:48.480
- So, 27.
- Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh. Ooh!

51:52.025 --> 51:53.151
It said they're invited.

51:53.652 --> 51:55.111
NINE × THREE = TWENTY-SEVEN

51:55.195 --> 51:57.614
That means the host
will require a table as well.

51:58.615 --> 52:00.158
TWENTY-SEVEN + HOST = TWENTY…

52:00.242 --> 52:01.743
Twenty-eight total.

52:01.827 --> 52:04.079
[both exclaim]

52:04.162 --> 52:06.039
Ooh, you're right,
you're right, you're right.

52:06.957 --> 52:08.959
TWENTY-EIGHT

52:09.459 --> 52:12.212
The next one's about knowing the streets
well enough to run errands.

52:13.004 --> 52:15.382
I'll… go try to find a map.

52:16.633 --> 52:18.802
HOW DO YOU WASH CLOTHES
THAT HAVE INK ON THEM?

52:19.469 --> 52:21.763
How should you wash clothes
with ink on them again?

52:21.847 --> 52:24.474
Shouldn't you just discard them?
Hey, Eunuch Oh.

52:25.517 --> 52:26.643
Your Highness.

52:26.726 --> 52:29.729
How are you supposed to wash clothes
that have been stained with ink again?

52:29.813 --> 52:31.898
For ink-stained clothes,
you need some hot rice paste.

52:31.982 --> 52:33.859
- First, you smear it on the--
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, that's it.

52:33.942 --> 52:34.901
Oh!

52:34.985 --> 52:35.986
Write it.

52:36.987 --> 52:38.572
Hot rice paste.

52:39.865 --> 52:41.700
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

52:41.783 --> 52:42.742
[Dang-gu exhales]

52:43.577 --> 52:44.870
I'm sure we got them all right.

52:45.370 --> 52:47.497
This was unexpected but interesting.

52:48.123 --> 52:50.458
And I am sure that Mu-deok will fail it.

52:52.544 --> 52:53.587
[laughs awkwardly]

52:53.670 --> 52:54.504
Uh…

52:54.588 --> 52:56.798
yeah, maybe we should probably find a way

52:56.882 --> 52:59.259
to deliver this perfect test sheet
to her right now.

53:00.760 --> 53:04.014
But how should we do it?
It'll look too obvious if we go.

53:05.265 --> 53:09.561
Perhaps if it's someone more conspicuous,
they won't be scrutinized as much.

53:11.187 --> 53:13.189
[upbeat music playing]

53:19.529 --> 53:20.488
Hmm?

53:25.452 --> 53:28.121
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

53:29.456 --> 53:30.373
[Mu-deok] This is hard.

53:31.291 --> 53:33.043
It's much harder than I thought.

53:35.086 --> 53:36.880
Hey, do not look at other people's papers.

53:40.258 --> 53:43.678
[eunuch] The Crown Prince is here!
Bow before him!

53:43.762 --> 53:45.055
[indistinct chatter]

53:46.389 --> 53:48.600
- [eunuch] Bow before him!
- [woman] Oh. Your Royal Highness!

53:48.683 --> 53:51.227
[indistinct chatter]

53:53.688 --> 53:55.023
[whimsical music playing]

53:57.776 --> 54:01.112
I heard there's a test.
I thought I'd offer some encouragement.

54:03.156 --> 54:04.699
We are honored, sire.

54:04.783 --> 54:07.869
[Go Won] Do not mind me.
Focus on your test.

54:12.499 --> 54:14.417
[whimsical music continues playing]

54:25.887 --> 54:26.805
Go back to work.

54:28.264 --> 54:29.307
Focus!

54:30.183 --> 54:31.393
[maidservant Park] Back to work.

54:31.476 --> 54:32.727
- And you too.
- Back--

54:33.353 --> 54:34.521
Go on and focus on something.

54:37.232 --> 54:38.066
[maidservant Park clears throat]

54:38.984 --> 54:40.986
[whimsical music continues playing]

55:10.682 --> 55:11.516
[drum pounding]

55:12.892 --> 55:14.269
[indistinct chatter]

55:16.438 --> 55:18.523
[maidservant Park]
I will now announce those of you

55:18.606 --> 55:20.650
who have passed the written test.

55:23.445 --> 55:26.322
Park Jun-hwa has passed.

55:27.115 --> 55:29.325
Lee Yeong-ok, failed.

55:29.409 --> 55:32.495
Hwang Yeon-ji, failed.

55:33.329 --> 55:35.123
Oh Jae-ho, passed.

55:37.959 --> 55:39.544
Number 125.

55:39.627 --> 55:40.962
Mu-deok.

55:41.546 --> 55:43.548
[epic music playing]

55:50.930 --> 55:52.348
[eunuch] Your Royal Highness!

55:52.432 --> 55:53.558
[pants]

55:54.684 --> 55:56.144
She passed it.

55:56.227 --> 55:57.771
- [all laugh]
- Yes! Oh, yes!

55:57.854 --> 55:59.773
All right! Yeah!
[laughs]

55:59.856 --> 56:01.232
[Dang-gu exclaims, laughs]

56:02.025 --> 56:02.859
[Go Won] Good work.

56:04.069 --> 56:07.822
[maidservant Park]
Forty of you have passed the written test.

56:08.323 --> 56:11.826
We shall now begin the practical.

56:14.412 --> 56:18.583
The practical test evaluates them on
their ability to carry out their duties.

56:19.584 --> 56:20.919
They'll prepare ingredients,

56:21.002 --> 56:23.838
clean, in addition to
washing dirty laundry.

56:23.922 --> 56:26.382
And last but not least,
they'll do a fitness test.

56:30.261 --> 56:31.096
[gong beats]

56:33.890 --> 56:36.184
[thrilling music playing]

56:55.703 --> 56:58.331
Number 125, Mu-deok.

56:58.414 --> 56:59.374
You passed.

56:59.916 --> 57:01.960
[thrilling music continues playing]

57:27.485 --> 57:28.319
Oh!

57:28.862 --> 57:30.947
Number 125, Mu-deok.

57:31.030 --> 57:32.365
You passed!

57:46.546 --> 57:48.840
[maidservant Park] Number 125, Mu-deok.

57:49.340 --> 57:50.675
You passed!

57:53.970 --> 57:56.514
[Dang-gu] Wow, Mu-deok is so impressive.

57:56.598 --> 57:58.391
There's only the fitness test left.

57:58.475 --> 57:59.976
We should go and cheer for her, right?

58:01.144 --> 58:04.063
I saw many fit individuals back there.

58:04.147 --> 58:06.399
I highly doubt that
she'll be in the top five.

58:06.483 --> 58:08.735
Sire, thank you for all of your help.

58:09.319 --> 58:10.278
[Seo Yul] Goodbye.

58:12.572 --> 58:14.699
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

58:17.243 --> 58:21.164
That was his way
of telling me not to come, right?

58:21.247 --> 58:23.666
Oh, goodness, why are they being so mean?

58:23.750 --> 58:25.251
Unbelievable!

58:26.878 --> 58:28.379
Whatever. Let us go.

58:29.255 --> 58:30.465
It is this way, Your Highness.

58:33.468 --> 58:35.303
- Yeah, I knew that. I did.
- Of course.

58:36.471 --> 58:39.349
[maidservant Park] From here,
you will travel five ri

58:39.432 --> 58:40.892
and bring back water.

58:40.975 --> 58:41.809
The winners…

58:43.102 --> 58:46.397
have to be the first five
to return with water.

58:47.649 --> 58:48.900
[Mu-deok] This is the last hurdle.

58:50.109 --> 58:51.778
I must be in the first five.

58:53.780 --> 58:55.823
[action music playing]

59:04.290 --> 59:05.875
- Begin.
- [drum beats]

59:05.959 --> 59:09.128
[candidates shout]

59:13.841 --> 59:15.426
He has not moved, he's just been staring

59:15.510 --> 59:16.844
at the book for days on end.

59:18.596 --> 59:19.472
Really?

59:27.981 --> 59:29.983
It can't be achieved overnight.

59:30.066 --> 59:31.526
You must have patience.

59:33.736 --> 59:34.571
Yes.

59:35.738 --> 59:39.033
Maidservant Kim is worried sick about you.

59:39.909 --> 59:41.703
Let me know if you need anything.

59:41.786 --> 59:45.957
I can prepare your bed, your food,
and clothing to your liking.

59:47.792 --> 59:49.210
I'll be all right.

59:58.469 --> 01:00:00.722
The wind is getting colder.

01:00:00.805 --> 01:00:02.807
[Jin] Keep the windows closed.

01:00:04.892 --> 01:00:08.938
Master Seo Gyeong originally wrote this
for a lady who could not see

01:00:09.022 --> 01:00:11.983
so that she would be able
to read it with her heart instead.

01:00:13.610 --> 01:00:14.902
I have one question.

01:00:16.321 --> 01:00:20.199
Did Master Seo Gyeong use to know
a woman who couldn't see?

01:00:24.162 --> 01:00:26.456
In the Great Chaos, centuries ago,

01:00:27.123 --> 01:00:29.375
the woman who stood
at Master Seo Gyeong's side

01:00:29.459 --> 01:00:31.836
was the very first leader of Jinyowon.

01:00:31.919 --> 01:00:34.881
And she was unable to see anything.

01:00:36.174 --> 01:00:38.092
[Jang Uk]
So the recipient of this love letter

01:00:38.176 --> 01:00:39.594
was the leader of Jinyowon.

01:00:41.721 --> 01:00:45.808
Are you sure that it's all right
if other people read this letter?

01:00:46.559 --> 01:00:48.603
What if these details
are his private life,

01:00:48.686 --> 01:00:50.772
and you're just requiring
everybody to read them?

01:00:52.482 --> 01:00:53.316
Hmm.

01:00:54.942 --> 01:00:57.820
You must be trying to use me
to figure out what is written in there.

01:00:58.488 --> 01:00:59.572
I will tell you this.

01:01:00.365 --> 01:01:05.411
Nothing written here is secret
or even at all something personal.

01:01:07.664 --> 01:01:09.874
Countless mages have been asked
to read this book,

01:01:09.957 --> 01:01:12.210
but no one knows it's a love letter.

01:01:12.794 --> 01:01:15.630
[Jang Uk] Right. He said that
no one knows it's a love letter.

01:01:15.713 --> 01:01:17.674
Instead of coming up with tricks,

01:01:17.757 --> 01:01:20.218
concentrate on training yourself.

01:01:21.010 --> 01:01:24.222
[Jang Uk] If it's a love letter,
how is it that no one knows?

01:01:29.268 --> 01:01:32.021
You can read it by training
your concentration skills.

01:01:32.563 --> 01:01:37.151
But now that you know what it is,
try to think of another way to read it.

01:01:37.985 --> 01:01:39.612
[Jang Uk] There must be
a different way to read it

01:01:39.696 --> 01:01:41.656
when you know that it's a love letter.

01:01:42.699 --> 01:01:44.867
A way those in training don't know.

01:01:44.951 --> 01:01:47.453
But those who know
it's a love letter can see.

01:01:48.037 --> 01:01:48.955
What could it be?

01:01:49.580 --> 01:01:52.667
How do you think
a love letter is supposed to begin?

01:02:03.720 --> 01:02:05.096
I have one last question.

01:02:06.097 --> 01:02:07.515
The first leader of Jinyowon,

01:02:08.766 --> 01:02:10.017
tell me what was her name.

01:02:22.864 --> 01:02:24.407
Love letters must always…

01:02:25.992 --> 01:02:27.869
begin with the name of the recipient.

01:02:28.786 --> 01:02:29.912
[Jin] Her name?

01:02:29.996 --> 01:02:33.666
Her surname was Jin,
and given name Seol-ran.

01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:37.003
The recipient's name was Jin Seol-ran.

01:02:37.086 --> 01:02:38.504
A blue orchid that blooms

01:02:39.881 --> 01:02:41.090
in white snow.

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:43.843
Her name will…

01:02:45.178 --> 01:02:47.054
help reveal this letter's context.

01:02:53.561 --> 01:02:55.897
[epic music playing]

01:03:25.551 --> 01:03:26.385
That's it.

01:03:29.013 --> 01:03:29.847
[exhales]

01:03:34.936 --> 01:03:36.938
Hey, hey, hey, Yul, look!

01:03:38.940 --> 01:03:40.566
There she goes, Mu-deok.

01:03:41.567 --> 01:03:42.985
[women yell]

01:03:45.112 --> 01:03:47.490
[soft music playing]

01:03:55.248 --> 01:03:56.666
[Jang Uk] "You cannot grasp water,

01:03:58.167 --> 01:03:59.502
but it's within the soil."

01:04:01.504 --> 01:04:02.880
"You cannot touch fire,

01:04:03.631 --> 01:04:04.924
but it is within the tree."

01:04:07.385 --> 01:04:08.886
"You cannot hold the wind…

01:04:10.888 --> 01:04:12.139
but it rests on the rock."

01:04:14.058 --> 01:04:17.687
"If you let them be,
they will be everywhere."

01:04:19.605 --> 01:04:21.607
"The faint, blue light

01:04:22.692 --> 01:04:24.026
makes me sigh."

01:04:26.863 --> 01:04:28.197
"My white breath

01:04:29.615 --> 01:04:31.826
turns into snow and gathers like tears."

01:04:32.952 --> 01:04:35.746
"So I cannot drop it but hide it away."

01:04:37.331 --> 01:04:39.834
"Despite knowing that
they will well up once again,

01:04:40.793 --> 01:04:45.089
"I am a fool
who dares not shed a single tear."

01:04:49.051 --> 01:04:49.886
[Dang-gu exhales]

01:04:50.428 --> 01:04:52.054
There are two back already.

01:04:54.682 --> 01:04:55.892
I don't see Mu-deok.

01:05:04.483 --> 01:05:05.943
[eunuch] There are six people
ahead of her.

01:05:06.652 --> 01:05:08.863
She needs to overtake
at least two of them to win.

01:05:15.703 --> 01:05:16.579
[grunts]

01:05:19.332 --> 01:05:22.418
I AM A FOOL
WHO DARES NOT SHED A SINGLE TEAR

01:05:29.717 --> 01:05:31.928
YOU CANNOT GRASP WATER
BUT IT IS INSIDE THE SOIL

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:39.644
[Sang-ho] Where are you going?

01:05:40.686 --> 01:05:41.520
Oh.

01:05:44.315 --> 01:05:45.399
I finished reading it.

01:05:57.870 --> 01:05:59.664
[crowd cheering]

01:06:01.123 --> 01:06:03.167
[crowd clapping]

01:06:04.669 --> 01:06:05.503
[groans]

01:06:07.838 --> 01:06:10.800
Number 29, Jang Jeong-do. You passed.

01:06:11.801 --> 01:06:14.011
And now, only one more remains.

01:06:14.553 --> 01:06:16.555
[thrilling music playing]

01:06:18.849 --> 01:06:20.351
[pants]

01:06:47.003 --> 01:06:49.088
[Mu-deok] I have no need
for a pupil who won't improve.

01:06:49.588 --> 01:06:51.674
If you're not going to do
anything, you should just die.

01:06:52.717 --> 01:06:54.719
Stop that! Damn! You just threw it.

01:06:54.802 --> 01:06:56.512
Don't act like you're still Naksu, okay?

01:07:03.352 --> 01:07:05.146
[Mu-deok] No matter how pathetic I feel,

01:07:06.230 --> 01:07:08.315
I must do what I can right now.

01:07:10.776 --> 01:07:12.653
If I am not willing to do anything,

01:07:14.238 --> 01:07:15.698
I might as well die.

01:07:20.661 --> 01:07:22.413
[crowd cheering]

01:07:24.665 --> 01:07:26.751
[shouting]

01:07:30.504 --> 01:07:32.131
[crowd cheering]

01:07:32.673 --> 01:07:34.175
[crowd applaud]

01:07:35.176 --> 01:07:37.053
Number 125, Mu-deok.

01:07:39.472 --> 01:07:40.806
You passed!

01:07:40.890 --> 01:07:42.433
[crowd applauding]

01:07:48.355 --> 01:07:49.940
YOU CANNOT GRASP WATER
BUT IT IS INSIDE THE SOIL

01:07:50.024 --> 01:07:52.735
It's word for word what is written
in the Words of the Heart.

01:07:53.527 --> 01:07:55.446
Jang Uk has done it.

01:07:57.865 --> 01:07:59.325
Jang Uk has done it?

01:08:04.163 --> 01:08:05.414
Where is he right now?

01:08:06.207 --> 01:08:07.333
He's at Sejukwon.

01:08:07.416 --> 01:08:10.711
The servant who was always with him
collapsed during the test,

01:08:10.795 --> 01:08:12.004
so he took her there, sir.

01:08:13.172 --> 01:08:14.006
His servant?

01:08:15.007 --> 01:08:16.967
- You mean his servant, Mu-deok?
- Yes.

01:08:17.051 --> 01:08:19.011
She was one of five
who passed the test today.

01:08:19.720 --> 01:08:21.931
She did faint as soon as
she reached the finish line,

01:08:22.014 --> 01:08:24.058
but still she-- she has made it.

01:08:24.767 --> 01:08:25.601
Really?

01:08:30.314 --> 01:08:33.651
[Jang Uk] All she did was risk her life
following the orders I gave.

01:08:34.360 --> 01:08:36.320
It was all because of me, sir.

01:08:48.749 --> 01:08:49.750
Now, I think…

01:08:51.836 --> 01:08:54.004
she was always at Uk's side.

01:08:56.048 --> 01:08:57.466
His servant, Mu-deok.

01:09:03.556 --> 01:09:07.184
The book was actually
Master Seo Gyeong's love letter.

01:09:10.062 --> 01:09:10.896
Really?

01:09:12.148 --> 01:09:14.233
Then why did he choose
to make it invisible?

01:09:14.984 --> 01:09:18.571
The woman he loved was blind.
He wanted her to read it with her heart.

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:21.407
That's so sweet.

01:09:21.991 --> 01:09:22.825
I don't think

01:09:23.868 --> 01:09:25.786
the letter actually reached her
in the end, though.

01:09:26.453 --> 01:09:28.414
If it had, it would be in Jinyowon,

01:09:29.290 --> 01:09:30.875
instead of being here at Songrim.

01:09:31.458 --> 01:09:34.628
A love letter that can't be seen
and was never sent?

01:09:35.838 --> 01:09:36.672
[scoffs]

01:09:36.755 --> 01:09:37.840
What a coward!

01:09:39.800 --> 01:09:42.136
He just wrote his feelings
and never told her.

01:09:43.637 --> 01:09:44.722
What a foolish…

01:09:46.348 --> 01:09:47.892
pitiful love letter.

01:09:53.522 --> 01:09:55.441
You're right. Love letters should be…

01:09:58.527 --> 01:10:00.362
delivered to the recipients like this.

01:10:01.822 --> 01:10:04.450
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

01:10:05.951 --> 01:10:07.286
That isn't a letter, though.

01:10:07.369 --> 01:10:08.704
And what is a letter?

01:10:08.787 --> 01:10:11.540
As long as it reveals your heart,
then it's a letter.

01:10:13.083 --> 01:10:15.586
[Mu-deok] Just wait there.
I'll be there soon, too.

01:10:15.669 --> 01:10:17.421
Be safe. Don't get caught.

01:10:26.805 --> 01:10:31.393
You must have felt
sorry for me… taking that exam.

01:10:31.977 --> 01:10:34.605
You were once
an incredibly powerful mage, so…

01:10:35.105 --> 01:10:36.815
of course, I did feel sorry for you.

01:10:37.858 --> 01:10:40.361
I suppose I taught you
something about loyalty.

01:10:40.444 --> 01:10:42.488
Seeing how far my master would go,

01:10:42.571 --> 01:10:45.950
I did think that I should be doing
my very best as your pupil.

01:10:48.244 --> 01:10:49.453
You must have felt pressured.

01:10:49.536 --> 01:10:51.664
Hmm. No, I didn't really.

01:10:52.331 --> 01:10:53.457
But I was conflicted

01:10:54.333 --> 01:10:57.127
if I should answer this letter
as your young master

01:10:57.211 --> 01:10:59.088
or if I should answer as your pupil,

01:10:59.672 --> 01:11:02.341
or just answer based on what I read.

01:11:08.264 --> 01:11:09.640
Well, what did you read?

01:11:10.724 --> 01:11:14.436
Should I answer
based on that, you think, also?

01:11:16.146 --> 01:11:17.564
Also? What?

01:11:18.148 --> 01:11:19.650
It's written right here.

01:11:19.733 --> 01:11:22.319
"This is how far I will go
just to be able to see you."

01:11:22.987 --> 01:11:26.282
"I'll do absolutely anything
if I can just see you."

01:11:26.907 --> 01:11:28.200
And this is my answer to that.

01:11:33.414 --> 01:11:37.876
[Mu-deok] I should have braced myself
before letting someone get this close.

01:11:42.006 --> 01:11:43.340
I missed you, too. A lot.

01:11:47.469 --> 01:11:48.637
That's my response.

01:11:58.022 --> 01:11:59.231
[Mu-deok] What I gave him…

01:12:01.275 --> 01:12:05.279
should not have been read
or even delivered.

01:12:07.281 --> 01:12:08.782
My foolish and pitiful…

01:12:10.576 --> 01:12:11.660
love letter.

01:12:17.374 --> 01:12:19.501
["You're Everything To Me"
by Shin Yong Jae playing]

01:12:43.567 --> 01:12:45.194
[Jang Uk] I miss you when I open my eyes.

01:12:45.277 --> 01:12:47.196
- I miss you every second they're open.
- Stop that.

01:12:47.279 --> 01:12:49.365
[Mu-deok] It seems that
you've already taken the poison.

01:12:49.448 --> 01:12:51.408
The antidote is
the person who poisons you.

01:12:51.492 --> 01:12:52.868
Are you out of your damn mind?

01:12:52.951 --> 01:12:54.828
It's just another symptom. I was poisoned?

01:12:54.912 --> 01:12:58.040
[Seo Yul] So the only one in your mind
has been Jang Uk, Naksu.

01:12:58.123 --> 01:13:00.250
It's not like you really believe
that I'm in love with you.

01:13:00.334 --> 01:13:02.294
Then do a better job
and make me believe it.

01:13:02.378 --> 01:13:04.838
[Mu-deok] That is the most precious thing
I've ever owned in my life.

01:13:04.922 --> 01:13:07.841
Please, try to win just once.
And win it back for me.

01:13:07.925 --> 01:13:10.719
Well, you see, I made a bet.
I made a bet with your servant there.

01:13:10.803 --> 01:13:13.013
[Mu-deok] Fight and perish, Jang Uk.

01:13:13.097 --> 01:13:14.181
[Jang Uk]
So this is what you meant that day

01:13:14.264 --> 01:13:15.682
when you told me that you had my weakness?

01:13:15.766 --> 01:13:17.101
Stop!

01:13:17.768 --> 01:13:21.397
[Jang Uk] I… I missed you too, a lot.
